            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for to disinfect, then the Mandarin for to care for the sick."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: hǎozhuǎn",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hǎozhuǎn — \"to take a turn for the better; to start to improve\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tā zhìliáo le yí ge yuè bìngqíng hǎozhuǎn le — He had treatment for a month, and his illness has taken a turn for the better."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two third tones meet in this word: hǎo is said with a rising tone before zhuǎn, and the spelling keeps both marks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hǎozhuǎn is built from 好 'good' and zhuǎn 'to turn', both inherited from Middle Chinese, xawX and trjwenX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second 'to move' and 'to turn round'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying how it was."
            }
          ]
        },
